# Everything the test suite needs *except* a pinned `tox`, so that the
# `oldest-tox` lock beside it can swap which `tox` the tests run
# against without restating the rest of the list.
#
# NOTE: `tox`'s `[testing]` extra provides `devpi-process` / `pytest`
# NOTE: (needed by the `tox.pytest` plugin) starting from v4.54.0. They
# NOTE: are listed here rather than left to the extra so that both
# NOTE: locks get them whichever `tox` they pin.
# Ref: https://github.com/tox-dev/tox/issues/3938
covdefaults
coverage
devpi-process
pytest
pytest-cov
pytest-subtests
pytest-xdist
# NOTE: v4.64.1 builds a real config-file loader for a section the
# NOTE: file lacks when a `-x` override targets one, so an override
# NOTE: aimed at `[testenv:lock-deps]` no longer reaches the seed
# NOTE: loader that exists to carry it. The plugin still behaves the
# NOTE: same -- its own workaround simply stops being reached, which
# NOTE: the 100% gate reads as dead code. The declared floor is
# NOTE: v4.55.1, so the workaround cannot just be deleted; deciding
# NOTE: what replaces the gate is its own change. Until then the lock
# NOTE: holds the last release the suite measures clean.
tox [testing] < 4.64.1
